uced on sir Ilya  and gained popularity and hangar Bay's  across the galaxy during the Galactic  Republic due to their ability to carry  weight far greater than their own  still the mando doesn't want the  Lloyd's working on his ship we've seen  him have a disdain for droids back in  Episode one when he specifically asked  for a human operated ship rather than a  droid one my guess as to why he hates  droids well they killed his parents back  in those flashbacks we saw Pelle uses a  device to analyze the extent of the  damage on the razor crest it's gonna be  quite the job considering the  Mandalorian won't let her use the droids  he only has 500 Imperial credits and we  know since the Empire has faded away the  value of imperial credits has  significantly dropped and that 500 will  only cover the cost of the hangar he  tells her he's good for it and we see  this payoff for her later on in the  episode as we venture deeper into moss  eisely we have these stormtrooper  helmets on spikes Tatooine was never a  planet that had much love for imperial  rule in Return of the Jedi we see  citizens of moss eisely celebrating the  fall of the empire back at the hangar  Pelle is playing a game of sabacc with  the droids you may remember SABIC as the  game young Han Solo played against Lando  Calrissian to win the Millennium Falcon  this game however seems a bit lower in  stakes betting small parts which we can  see on the table their game is  interrupted when a loud noise emanates  from the ship it's just a child who  Pelle picks up and we'll let her charge  mando extra for babysitting one of the  interesting things about moss eisely in  the Mandalorian is that it's far less  populated it seems as though Tatooine  has fallen on hard times like much of  the galaxy even the cantina which was  filled in a new hope has only a  spattering of patrons this could  possibly be because the droid who runs  the place tells mando that the bounty  guild no longer operates on Tatooine  which