d fennec when she told  him that the Mandalorian was wanted by  the bounty hunters guild wanted so much  so in fact that his head would give him  even more clout than hers in the dune  see they stopped to deal with the  Tuscans they almost magically appear  behind Toro like they did to Luke in a  new hope thankfully the mando knows how  to communicate with them Trading Toros  binoculars for safe passage beyond the  dunes they stop yet again when they come  across a lone do back with a dead bounty  hunter attached it's likely this guy was  also searching for fennec judging by his  tracking fob and was also shot down by  her the investigation is short-lived as  mando is shot by an MK sniper rifle a  shot he probably wouldn't have survived  if it weren't for his best car steal the  Mandalorian is able to get to safety and  he suggests they wait till night to  stand a better chance of getting a  fennec the problem is she has the high  ground his plan involves using flash  charges to briefly stun Finnick giving  them enough time to reach the ridge  without getting shot the Mandalorian is  hit yet again and flies into the sand  man he is not having a good day  but before fennec can get a lethal shot  she's held at gunpoint by Toro they have  a brief battle fennec being the more  experienced fighter but the Mandalorian  intervenes and they are able to cuff her  she asks if he's the Mandalorian that  caused the big uproar on Navarro this is  the first time we're given the name of  that volcanic planet we saw in episodes  1 &amp; 3 where the Mandalorian fought off  the bounty hunters guild apparently word  has spread of his exploits with only one  working speeder the Mandalorian offers  to go back in search of the Dewback  leaving Toro with fennec then accuses  this opportunity to sway Toro if its  entry into the guild he wants what  better capture than the Mandalorian  getting him would make him legendary  heck his armor alone is worth more than  her bounty and he would be 